```

Two honest limits. The Map lives in one isolate's memory, so each isolate counts separately and the effective global limit is higher than the number you set. And a fixed window allows a burst of up to twice the limit across a boundary.

For a strict shared limit you need Durable Objects. For abuse protection this is enough. Size the limit to real usage: a single page load can fire hundreds of asset requests, so a proxy path needs a far higher ceiling than a login path.

